 plugin would make the witness and the PR test test/shell.d/notifications-test.sh observed; mirrors do not change test commands.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/notifications-card-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/shell.d/notifications-test.sh","kind":"file","line":183},{"id":"tests_pass","kind":"check"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Disclosures test_outcome_unobserved / test_results_not_joined: the witness test is not run by an audit test command","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/notifications/NotificationLogic.js:sanitizeBody"],"scenario":"a notification from app Chromium whose body is just 'github.com/omacom/omarchy can you review?' (no origin link, no plain-text origin): the card shows 'can you review?'"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Unchanged by this PR: when the body has no origin link, the plain-text replacement removes a leading web address and the white space after it. That is right for the origin Chromium sends as plain text to a server without hyperlinks, but a Chromium-based app that sends a message with no origin at all (a web app or extension notification, if Chromium omits the origin) would still lose a first word that looks like a web address. The shell's server takes hyperlinks, so a page notification arrives with the link; whether any Chromium path sends no origin is not shown here.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/notifications/NotificationLogic.js","kind":"file","line":105},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-DHZ3","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: a body without an origin link still loses a leading web address","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Chromium notification with no origin at all\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/notifications/NotificationLogic.js:sanitizeBody"],"scenario":"a web notification from http://127.0.0.1:8123 with message 'hello': the card shows '127.0.0.1:8123' then 'hello'"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"An origin link to localhost, an IP address or a host shown with non-ASCII letters (an IDN) does not match the link expression, so the card shows the link text before the message, before and after this PR. Out of scope for this fix; noted so a maintainer can decide whether to widen the expression.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/corpus/lifecycle/notify-link-origin-kept.events","kind":"test"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-261004-74P8","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: origin links that are not a dotted ASCII host stay in the card","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Web notification from localhost / an IP / an IDN host in the live shell\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (disclosure effects_unavailable), so call-path statements come from reading the code: NotificationCard.qml calls sanitizeBody (visibility of the body line) and styledBody (the rendered text); nothing else calls them.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/notifications/components/NotificationCard.qml","kind":"file","line":47}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for QML/JS here","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Evaluated 1fb5c657 = baseline quattro-proof 58cd8018 + the upstream commit 1e9ffb09 (identical lines) + proof work: NotificationLogic.j